export default {"T003568":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Faithful flatness gives a pure ring map</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000209\"><span>Faithfully flat ring map</span><code>P000209</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T003568\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T003568</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000498\"><span>Ring map universally injective on underlying modules</span><code>P000498</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Ring homomorphisms</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The map <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mo>⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M\\to M\\otimes_R S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> becomes split injective after extension of scalars; faithful flatness reflects that injectivity.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08WP\">Stacks 08WP · numbered assertion and proof · Stacks 08WP · universal injectivity</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/descent/#tag-08WP\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T003568\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T003568\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T003569":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Module descent implies effective module descent</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000933\"><span>Descent morphism for modules</span><code>P000933</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T003569\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T003569</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000934\"><span>Effective descent morphism for modules</span><code>P000934</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Ring homomorphisms</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> For a commutative ring map either condition is equivalent to purity of its underlying module map.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08XA\">Stacks 08XA · numbered assertion and proof · Stacks 08XA · (a) iff (b)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/descent/#tag-08XA\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://ftp.gwdg.de/pub/misc/EMIS/journals/TAC/volumes/7/n3/n3.pdf\">B. Mesablishvili, Pure morphisms of commutative rings are effective descent morphisms for modules, Theorem 4</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T003569\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T003569\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T003570":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Effective module descent is purity</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000934\"><span>Effective descent morphism for modules</span><code>P000934</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T003570\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T003570</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000498\"><span>Ring map universally injective on underlying modules</span><code>P000498</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Ring homomorphisms</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Character duality identifies purity with a split condition. Applying the descent comparison yields equivalence precisely in that case.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08XA\">Stacks 08XA · numbered assertion and proof · Stacks 08XA · (b) iff (c)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/descent/#tag-08XA\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://ftp.gwdg.de/pub/misc/EMIS/journals/TAC/volumes/7/n3/n3.pdf\">B. Mesablishvili, Pure morphisms of commutative rings are effective descent morphisms for modules, Theorem 4</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T003570\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T003570\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>"};
